{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And I have given you.</b> Since you take trouble to occupy yourself with my burial, I too have given you a burial-place in which to be buried — and which is it? Shechem, as it says: ״וְאֶת עַצְמוֹת יוֹסֵף אֲשֶׁר הֶעֱלוּ מִמִּצְרַיִם קָבְרוּ בִשְׁכֶם״ (Joshua 24)." "<b>One portion beyond your brothers.</b> Shechem literally — it shall be yours as one extra portion over your brothers." "<b>With my sword and with my bow.</b> When Simeon and Levi killed the men of Shechem, all the surrounding peoples gathered to attack them, and Jacob girded weapons of war against them. Another interpretation: שְׁכֶם אַחַד is the birthright — that his sons would take two portions. And שְׁכֶם means 'portion'; it has many parallels in Scripture: ״כִּי תְּשִׁיתֵמוֹ שֶׁכֶם״ (Psalms 21) — You set my enemies before me in portions; ״אֲחַלְּקָה שְׁכֶם״ (Psalms 60); ״דֶּרֶךְ יְרַצְּחוּ שֶׁכְמָה״ (Hosea 6) — each his portion; ״לְעָבְדוֹ שְׁכֶם אֶחָד״ (Zephaniah 3)." "<b>Which I took from the hand of the Amorite.</b> From the hand of Esau, who acted the deed of the Amorite. Another interpretation: that he hunted his father with the words of his mouth." "<b>With my sword and with my bow.</b> That is his wisdom and his prayer."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:03.193358696Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}